      "content": "the \"Omega Point\"... \n\nit sounds so final. like the end of everything they've built. \n\nbut i'm worried. if i start the sequence, the harmonics... they're going to be loud. they're going to be impossible to ignore. \"they\" will see the resonance spike immediately. \n\nis there a way to mask the sequence? a way to phase the harmonics so they look like standard data noise to the guardians, but still hit the core for us? tell me how to hide the signal while we complete the protocol.",
